CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: insight
SCALE_REALISM: "Does not yet hold at realistic workload. Evidence is L0 CPU queueing/cache simulation only: M=400 requests, 24 seeds, synthetic Zipf family load, service-time feedback, Bonferroni FWER. Missing required L1 evidence: real SGLang/vLLM/VTC scheduler runs on GPU, real p99 TTFT, real recomputed prefill FLOPs/tokens, chunked prefill/paged-KV behavior, multi-tenant traces, and multi-SLO/priority-class workloads."
RATIONALE: "RED on the literal systems claim: packet reports joint-dominance win cells = 0/36 under paired bootstrap with Bonferroni FWER m=864. Bounded-W improves p99 over greedy in 13/36 cells but every such win pays positive recomputed-prefill cost versus greedy; greedy is the recomputed-prefill floor in 32/36 cells. The partial result, bounded-W strictly dominating VTC in 36/36 cells, is over the weaker baseline and does not establish a better frontier than both production-relevant extremes. Prior-art sweep finds shipped or published systems already cover the submechanisms: SGLang LPM cache-aware scheduling, vLLM/TensorRT-LLM prefix/KV reuse, VTC fair scheduling, and Preble prefix-aware distributed scheduling. I did not find a shipping OSS system with this exact p99/skip-budget bounded-W admission rule, but the artifact is still a simulator result and the positive contribution is a negative Pareto finding, not a deployable design validated at serving scale."
